---
title: MCP
description: Connect your own AI agent to nullish over MCP.
---

nullish exposes its actions as MCP tools, the same ones its built-in assistant uses. Connect any MCP-capable agent or client, like Claude, ChatGPT or your own, and do your bookkeeping from there.

- Server: `https://api.nullish.ch/mcp`
- Transport: streamable HTTP
- Authentication: an API key, as a bearer token

## Create an API key

{% steps %}

1. In nullish, open the menu with your name and go to **API keys**, then choose **Create API key**.

2. Give it a **Name**, pick an **Expiration**, and choose **MCP server** as the **Resource**.

3. Pick the **Access**: **Read** gives your agent the tools that look things up, **Read and write** gives it all of them.

4. Copy the key. It isn't shown again.

{% /steps %}

## Connect your client

With Claude Code:

```sh
claude mcp add --transport http nullish https://api.nullish.ch/mcp \
  --header "Authorization: Bearer nullish_…"
```

With clients configured in JSON:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "nullish": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://api.nullish.ch/mcp",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer nullish_…"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

{% aside %}
Your agent works with your own access, across all your organizations, and your
[role](/en/team/#roles) still applies. Delete the key and it loses access immediately.
{% /aside %}
